nodecode-corpus is a rewrite of teakesdev's teakesdev/corpus-agent-kit:

  https://github.com/teakesdev/corpus-agent-kit
  commit 53db664236201a885a3a7133ffe62476293faace
  Apache-2.0 (LICENSE); its copyright line is the stock placeholder
  "Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]" and the repository names no
  holder, so the holder is taken as the author's GitHub handle, teakesdev.

The original carries no code: it is one MCP server citation
(https://corpuslaw.us/api/mcp, streamable HTTP) plus two prose skills, one for
US-law research and one for a company-formation intake, wrapped for several
harnesses. What was rewritten here is that server spoken to directly from the
image -- a small JSON-RPC client (initialize, notifications/initialized,
tools/call, a plain JSON or an event-stream answer, one session per start, an
optional bearer key) in mcp.lisp, five model tools named after the catalog's own
(law_search, law_get_node, law_coverage, corpus_account, and corpus_call for the
rest, the formation family included), a /corpus command, and a primer in
tools.lisp that condenses the two skills' procedure: search before answering,
quote the citation verbatim, read the provision, check coverage instead of
guessing, quote limits and prices only from live responses, never collect a
Social Security Number, never promise to file, pay or submit, and treat referral
codes as the vendor's business. What was left out, and why: the two skills are
not shipped as files, so the per-harness config tables (useless inside a cell),
the worked examples and the vendor's own marketing copy, including the copy it
required before a formation question, are gone -- their doctrine is the primer,
in our own words; the other wrapper folders and the logo are decoration or a
second spelling of the same manifest.
